B.a_P=new A.fS("The Chariot","Katha Upanishad 1.3.3\u20134","Know the Self as the lord of the chariot, the body as the chariot, the intellect as the charioteer, and the mind as the reins. The senses, they say, are the horses; the objects of the senses, the roads.","\u0906\u0924\u094d\u092e\u093e\u0928\u0902 \u0930\u0925\u093f\u0928\u0902 \u0935\u093f\u0926\u094d\u0927\u093f \u0936\u0930\u0940\u0930\u0902 \u0930\u0925\u092e\u0947\u0935 \u0924\u0941 \u0964\n\u092c\u0941\u0926\u094d\u0927\u093f\u0902 \u0924\u0941 \u0938\u093e\u0930\u0925\u093f\u0902 \u0935\u093f\u0926\u094d\u0927\u093f \u092e\u0928\u0903 \u092a\u094d\u0930\u0917\u094d\u0930\u0939\u092e\u0947\u0935 \u091a \u0965","Autopilot is the horses running the chariot while the charioteer sleeps. You are not the horses, not the chariot \u2014 you are the one riding. Awareness wakes the charioteer.","Next time you reach for something automatically, ask: who is holding the reins right now?","assets/images/chariot.jpg")
B.a_T=new A.fS("Lift Yourself by Yourself","Bhagavad Gita 6.5","Let a person lift the self by the Self; let them not lower the self. For the Self alone is the friend of the self, and the Self alone is its enemy.","\u0909\u0926\u094d\u0927\u0930\u0947\u0926\u093e\u0924\u094d\u092e\u0928\u093e\u0924\u094d\u092e\u093e\u0928\u0902 \u0928\u093e\u0924\u094d\u092e\u093e\u0928\u092e\u0935\u0938\u093e\u0926\u092f\u0947\u0924\u094d \u0964","No one can do this for you \u2014 not a teacher, not an app. The same mind that traps you is the one that frees you, depending on who is in charge of it.","Speak to yourself once today the way you would speak to a friend you believe in.","assets/images/freedom.jpg")
B.a0_=new A.fS("Practice and Letting Go","Bhagavad Gita 6.35","Undoubtedly the mind is restless and hard to restrain. But by practice (abhy\u0101sa) and by non-attachment (vair\u0101gya) it is held.","\u0905\u092d\u094d\u092f\u093e\u0938\u0947\u0928 \u0924\u0941 \u0915\u094c\u0928\u094d\u0924\u0947\u092f \u0935\u0948\u0930\u093e\u0917\u094d\u092f\u0947\u0923 \u091a \u0917\u0943\u0939\u094d\u092f\u0924\u0947 \u0965","Even Arjuna said the mind is like the wind. Krishna doesn't deny it \u2014 he gives two tools: come back again and again, and stop clinging to what pulls you.","Count how many times you come back today, not how many times you wander.","assets/images/waves.jpg")
B.a_O=new A.fS("Who am I?","Ramana Maharshi, N\u0101n Y\u0101r",'The thought "Who am I?" will destroy all other thoughts, and like the stick used for stirring the burning pyre, it will itself in the end get destroyed.',"",'When a thought arises, ask: to whom did it arise? "To me." Then: who am I? Attention turns from the thought to its source \u2014 the awareness that was never a thought.','Do three minutes of the "Who am I?" practice. When a thought comes, ask "to whom?"',"assets/images/witness.jpg")
B.a_X=new A.fS("Knowing the Breath","Satipa\u1e6d\u1e6dh\u0101na Sutta (MN 10)",'Breathing in long, one knows: "I breathe in long." Breathing out short, one knows: "I breathe out short."',"","Not controlling \u2014 knowing. Mindfulness is simply knowing what is happening while it is happening.","For ten breaths, just know whether each one is long or short.","assets/images/breath.jpg")
B.a_Z=new A.fS("The Space","Often attributed to Viktor Frankl","Between stimulus and response there is a space. In that space is our power to choose our response. In our response lies our growth and our freedom.","","Autopilot is when the space collapses and stimulus becomes response. Every pause you take widens the space a little.","Use The Pause once today, at the exact moment you feel pulled.","assets/images/bridge.jpg")
B.a_R=new A.fS("The Last Freedom","Viktor Frankl, Man's Search for Meaning","Everything can be taken from a man but one thing: the last of the human freedoms \u2014 to choose one's attitude in any given set of circumstances, to choose one's own way.","","Written after the camps. If attitude could be chosen there, it can be chosen in traffic.","Pick one annoyance today and consciously choose your attitude toward it.","assets/images/road.jpg")
B.a_U=new A.fS("The Evening Review","Seneca, On Anger 3.36","When the light has been taken away and my wife has fallen silent, I examine my whole day and go back over what I have done and said, hiding nothing from myself, passing nothing by.","","The Stoics reviewed each day without self-punishment, like a kind teacher marking work. What you review at night, you notice by day.","Do tonight's evening review in the Journal tab.","assets/images/evening_sea.jpg")
B.a_Y=new A.fS("The Inner Citadel","Marcus Aurelius, Meditations (paraphrase)","You have power over your mind \u2014 not outside events. Realise this, and you will find strength.","","Events are the weather. Your response is the house you live in.",'When something goes wrong today, say: "This is weather. What is mine to do?"',"assets/images/stones.jpg")
B.a_W=new A.fS("Right Beside You","Kabir","Where do you search for me, O seeker? I am right beside you \u2014 not in temple, not in mosque, not in rituals. Seek truly and you will find me in a moment's search.","\u092e\u094b\u0915\u094b \u0915\u0939\u093e\u0901 \u0922\u0942\u0901\u0922\u0947 \u0930\u0947 \u092c\u0928\u094d\u0926\u0947, \u092e\u0948\u0902 \u0924\u094b \u0924\u0947\u0930\u0947 \u092a\u093e\u0938 \u092e\u0947\u0902 \u0964","What you are looking for is not elsewhere. It is the one who is looking.","Stop for one moment and feel that you exist \u2014 before any thought about it.","assets/images/reflection.jpg")
B.a_N=new A.fS("Self-Remembering","G. I. Gurdjieff (as taught by P. D. Ouspensky)","Remember yourself always and everywhere.","",'Divided attention: aware of what you are doing and aware that you are the one doing it. "I am here, washing this cup."','During one ordinary task, silently say: "I am here, doing this."',"assets/images/mudra.jpg")
B.a_V=new A.fS("Making It Conscious","Attributed to C. G. Jung","Until you make the unconscious conscious, it will direct your life and you will call it fate.","","Autopilot isn't fate \u2014 it is unseen habit. The Inner Map exists to make it seen.","Open the Map tab and read your reflections slowly.","assets/images/glass.jpg")
B.a_S=new A.fS("Clouds in the Sky","Thich Nhat Hanh","Feelings come and go like clouds in a windy sky. Conscious breathing is my anchor.","","You are the sky. Feelings are weather passing through it.","When a strong feeling comes, name it and take three conscious breaths.","assets/images/night_sky.jpg")
B.a_Q=new A.fS("The Five Sheaths","Taittiriya Upanishad 2","Within the body made of food is another, made of breath; within it, one made of mind; within it, one made of understanding; within it, one made of bliss.","","The Inner Map uses these five layers. Awareness travels inward from body to breath to mind to wisdom to joy \u2014 and the witness of all five is what you are.","Look at which sheath is dimmest on your Map, and feed it today.","assets/images/cosmos.jpg")
B.r3=s([B.a_P,B.a_T,B.a0_,B.a_O,B.a_X,B.a_Z,B.a_R,B.a_U,B.a_Y,B.a_W,B.a_N,B.a_V,B.a_S,B.a_Q],A.aA("H<fS>"))
B.S4=new A.i(0,2)
B.Eb=new A.e_(0.75,B.dj,B.p4,B.S4,1.5)
B.P_=s([B.Eb],t.sq)
B.Xh=new A.dZ("S","Stop","Whatever you are doing \u2014 stop. Let your hands be still. Nothing needs to happen for one minute.")
B.X6=new A.dZ("T","Take a breath","One slow breath in through the nose\u2026 and a longer breath out. Then another. Feel the air.")
B.Xf=new A.dZ("O","Observe","What is here? A feeling \u2014 name it. A thought \u2014 see it as a thought. The body \u2014 where is it tight?")
B.Xg=new A.dZ("P","Proceed","Now choose. Not the habit's next move \u2014 yours. What would the witness do next?")
B.r4=s([B.Xh,B.X6,B.Xf,B.Xg],t.iT)
B.a5x=new A.aP("Stories",null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null)
B.El=new A.l1(0,B.mh,B.a5x,t.lM)
B.K2=new A.bv(61075,"MaterialIcons",!1)
B.KJ=new A.c7(B.K2,null,null,null,null)
B.a5d=new A.aP("Articles",null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null)
B.Ek=new A.l1(1,B.KJ,B.a5d,t.lM)
B.P4=s([B.El,B.Ek],t.OV)
B.h_=s([B.dI,B.cO,B.hQ,B.hR,B.ky],t.QP)
B.r5=s([u.X,"Is it hot or cold? Tight or buzzing? Just describe it.","Breathe into the place where it lives. Let the breath surround it.","Notice: the urge is a sensation, not a command.","It is rising, or peaking, or already falling. Watch which.","You don't have to act and you don't have to fight. Only watch.","Every wave you ride without obeying makes the next one smaller.","What does the urge promise? Has it ever kept that promise?"],t.s)
